    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the July 3rd slate with **Yordan Alvarez** leading the charge, boasting our highest efficiency score of 82.21. Facing Martinez, he holds an elite xwOBA of 0.477, and with a favorable SP_xERA of 4.72, he is poised for a massive outing. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.98) follows closely behind, benefiting from a prime leadoff spot and a technical edge against Pallante; his scoring is buoyed by a 4% bonus for the pitcher's slow delivery, which creates an ideal environment for him to exploit the stolen base category, our primary area of focus. **Christian Yelich** also earns a strong recommendation (75.84), leveraging a significant platoon advantage against Cabrera to anchor the top of the lineup.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision today was keeping **Luke Raley** on the bench. Despite a solid base projection, his score of 39.35 fell just shy of our 40.0 efficiency floor, primarily due to a challenging matchup against Cease and his 3.01 xERA. We opted to prioritize the high-upside platoon edges of **Casey Schmitt** (63.92) and **Carson Benge** (63.98), both of whom capitalize on favorable park factors and mid-4.00 xERA opposition. While **Kazuma Okamoto** and **Caleb Durbin** landed in the marginal-to-strong transition zone, we are maintaining faith in their lineup placement and recent form to provide steady contributions across the board. We will continue to monitor the status of **Trea Turner**, who remains unavailable today, and ensure we remain vigilant regarding any late-breaking weather alerts that could threaten the viability of our projected starts.",
